From 024cb6ea7605626c082272ed41e4ca227369ad75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johann Felfer <31707158+HansFel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:39:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(motion): 2D Contour tab width is the bridge that
 stays, not the centre-path gap

The tab window on the tool-centre ring was the tab width alone. The
cutter disc bites D/2 past each window end, so the bridge was only
tab_width - D wide on the channel centre line, and a tab width of D or
less left no bridge: the part came free with no message. The window is
now the tab width plus the tool diameter (ring::tab_window), and a
tabbed level whose windows fill the whole loop says so in the notes.

Tests: contour_tabs.rs measures the bridge as the swept disc of the
posted feeds against the centre ring. machining2d.rs: the tabbed-level
length takes the longer windows; two inside-contour tests used four
6 mm tabs with a 10 mm tool on a 40 mm ring (physically no tab could
stand) and now use two 4 mm tabs. The first-router-part demo is
regenerated (WRITE_GOLDEN=1).

Fixes #2480

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
