From 613ba4abf39623762cf03b363c42107b69fc4994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:12:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(motion): tab bridge holds at corners and with leads

The tab rule is now on the true material. The smallest distance
between the swept discs on the two sides of a tab, leads included,
must be at least the tab width W.

Two review blockers showed that the centre-line window of W + D did
not hold this rule:

- B1: at a corner the chord between the window ends is shorter than
  the arc length, so the true neck fell under W (an inside 10x10
  corner gave -0.10 mm, no bridge).
- B2: Linear, Arc and Tangential leads reach back into the tab
  window (Linear 4 with W 3 gave -5 mm).

New module tab_bridge.rs: fit_tabs grows each window in bounded
rounds (64 at most). Each round measures the distance between the
keep tail (walk suffix and lead-out) and the next keep head (lead-in
and walk prefix), and grows the window by the shortfall. If the
windows fill the loop, a visible "tabs:" note is kept. The fit is
cached per ring for each band.

Pins: contour_tab_bridge.rs (inside corner, picked start on a corner
with W 4 and 1.5, bore, every lead family with W 3/6/10, inside and
conventional). Three old pins and the first-router-part example
cache follow the wider windows.

Refs #2480

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
